---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const stack = [
  ['Astro 7', 'Static site generation, routing, content collections, Markdown rendering'],
  ['Tailwind CSS 4', 'Styling through the official Vite plugin and the Typography plugin for Markdown'],
  ['React 19', 'One interactive island: the post search on the blog page'],
  ['@astrojs/rss', 'RSS feed generated from the blog collection'],
  ['@astrojs/sitemap', 'sitemap-index.xml generated at build time'],
  ['WordPress REST API', 'Headless content source fetched at build time'],
];
---

<Layout title="About" description="What this site is and how it is built.">
  <article class="prose max-w-3xl">
    <h1>About this site</h1>
    <p>
      Astro Field Notes is a reference project that accompanies the article
      <a href={url(`/blog/astro-explained`)}>Astro, explained by someone who just built a site with it</a>.
      It exists to show, with running code, what Astro does differently from a traditional CMS or a single-page app framework.
    </p>
    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{stack.map(([name, role]) => <tr><td>{name}</td><td>{role}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>Where to look in the source</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>src/content.config.ts</code> defines the blog collection and its schema.</li>
      <li><code>src/content/blog/</code> holds the posts as Markdown.</li>
      <li><code>src/pages/blog/[id].astro</code> turns each post into a static page.</li>
      <li><code>src/components/PostSearch.tsx</code> is the only component that runs in the browser.</li>
      <li><code>src/lib/wordpress.ts</code> talks to the WordPress REST API.</li>
      <li><code>src/styles/themes.css</code> and <code>src/lib/themes.ts</code> define the five themes.</li>
      <li><code>.github/workflows/deploy.yml</code>, <code>netlify.toml</code>, <code>vercel.json</code> and <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> cover deployment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The source is on <a href="https://github.com/fareezahmed/astro-blog">GitHub</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
